    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000026",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -980,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 1180,
        "content": "## Monitor many endpoints, retry before alerting, and report once a day\n\n**Who's it for**\n\nAnyone running services or automations that other work depends on, who would rather not hear from a customer that something broke on Friday \u2014 and who has stopped reading alert channels because they cry wolf.\n\n### How it works\n\nEvery five minutes the workflow walks a list of endpoints. Each is called with **Never Error** switched on, so a 500, a timeout or a dead tunnel arrives as ordinary data instead of killing the run. A monitor that dies with the thing it watches tells nobody.\n\nA Code node then decides what healthy means \u2014 status code plus, optionally, one field that must be true in the body. Without that check, Never Error would make every response look like a success, including an HTML error page.\n\n**One failed request is not an outage.** A failure waits 30 seconds and asks again. Only a confirmed failure counts, which removes most of the noise that makes people mute channels.\n\nState is kept per endpoint, so you hear about the *change*: one message going down, one coming back with the minutes in between, and an escalation after six failed checks in a row. Each morning a digest reports what is still broken, and stays quiet when nothing is.\n\n### Setup\n\n1. Edit **Endpoints to watch** \u2014 name, url, and the field that proves health (null accepts any 2xx/3xx).\n2. Connect Slack on the three alert nodes and pick channels.\n3. Optional: connect Google Sheets on **Append to outage log** for a history.\n\n### Customization tips\n\nReplace the Endpoints node with Google Sheets if the list lives elsewhere. Swap Slack for Teams, email or your ticket system. The escalation threshold sits in **Still down long enough to escalate?**"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000027",
      "name": "Section: the loop",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -40,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## 1. Walk the list and ask\nEach endpoint is called on its own, with Never Error, so an outage arrives as data instead of killing the run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000028",
      "name": "Section: confirm",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        880,
        220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 680,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 2. Ask twice before waking anyone\nA single failure waits 30 seconds and is retried. Only a confirmed failure counts as an outage."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029",
      "name": "Section: speak on change",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1560,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "## 3. Speak only when something changes\nState is kept per endpoint: one message going down, one coming back, an escalation after six failures in a row."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000030",
      "name": "Section: digest",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -440,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1060,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## 4. One quiet summary a day\nAt 08:00 the digest reports what is still broken. If nothing is, it says nothing at all."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
